some span the stars some  pound the pavement and some work outside  of reality altogether  but all of these superhero teams shared  one thing in common they'd be right at  home on the silver screen  these are the dc teams we'd like to see  in the dc  eu sometimes known as the international  club of heroes the batman of all nations  debuted back in 1955.  in detective comics number 215 the  legend of batman has spread so widely  across the world that imitators have  emerged  and everywhere from argentina to italy  the knight  and the squire clean up crime in england  the gaucho rides through the streets of  argentina  protecting them from vicious criminals  the musketeer takes down parisian  nerdwells in a plumed chapeau this  is straight up silver aged comic book  story stuff  right down to the night and squires  horse-shaped motorcycles  you might think this would be a hard  sell for modern audiences  but the batman of all nations popped up  in 2007's batman number 667  and the concept is as fresh today as it  was the year it made its debut  with just a little fine tuning the idea  of batman styled vigilantes the world  over would fit  smoothly into the dc universe the dc  eu's world is a highly interconnected  one  with its modern day global conversation  moving at the light speed pace of social  media  in fact it might be stranger to imagine  a world where there  aren't batman imitators bring on the  batman from every corner of the globe  and let them redefine their group once  more this time  for dc's movie fans just don't invite  this guy  what gives you the right what's the  difference between you and me  i'm not wearing hockey pads  not every incarnation of the teen titans  has been a rousing success  but every single one has at least been  pretty interesting  the very first lineup referred to in  earnest as the fab foursome  hey it was the 60s you'd have loved it  at the time  the soap opera melodrama that was the  1980s new  teen titans who doesn't want their super  powered teenagers served with the sight  of angst romance and betrayal  and then there's the 2003 cartoon you  can bet  any money that an entire generation has  that theme song  permanently stuck in their heads most  recently  is the wacky wonderland that is teen  titans go  which has been running for an impressive  seven years now the point  is the teen titans are arguably one of  the best ideas dc has ever had  every lineup sizzles with storytelling  possibility  and it's a big help that the titans are  also already familiar property to many  fans  what with the last two decades worth of  smash hit cartoons in the dc universe  original series  so why not just go ahead and bring that  goodwill into the dc eu  and hey if nothing else who doesn't want  to see the titans try to explain why a  t-shaped tower isn't a disastrous idea  to robert pattinson's steely-eyed batman  originally the seven soldiers were a  golden age super team who took on the  axis in world war ii  then in 2005 writer grant morrison and a  roster of artists revamped the team into  something entirely different  and genuinely wonderful to boot seven  soldiers of victory chronicles  seven reluctant second string heroes  strange journey to coming together as a  team to fight the fiendish  shida an earth-inhabiting race of the  far future  what ultimately makes the story so  tremendously unique is its format  the series consists of two bookend  issues and between them  seven four-issue character-specific arcs  though every hero fights the shita they  do so separately  even in the climactic final battle they  can't really comprehend the larger  picture of what they are doing  in the end the seven soldiers are a team  who aren't  in fact much of a team at all this is a  balancing act of a book and one that  would admittedly  challenge any filmmaker no matter how  skilled they may be  but the comic pulled it off proving how  great the reward is for taking on the  risk of the premise  and a movie could succeed in much the  same way  it helps that the seven soldiers include  some of dc's most colorful characters  like zatanna and mr miracle they're all  a little weird  being rooted in their own particular  corners of the dc universe  swept up in dramas utterly unknown to  everyone else in the story  combining their unique paths into one  complete  satisfying big screen arc would  definitely be a challenge  but one that would be well worth  undertaking  the zoo crew is a band of  anthropomorphic animals from earth sea  a parallel planet home to places like  mew orleans  and pigsburg that'll do pig  that'll do the team's leader  is captain carrot known to most as mild  maynard  roger a humble cartoonist toiling away  in  new york city then superman crashed into  his reality and accidentally  irradiated the carrots growing in  roger's window box  one bite later and roger was bunny  hopping his way across the city  hearing noises from miles away and  discovering he had the strength  of a whole warren's worth of rabbits the  zoo crew  ended up being dc's last funny animal  property  but boy did they make it count and sure  you might not think such a wacky  childlike group has a place in the dc eu  but remember this it can get weirder  i just wash my hands that's why they're  wet  no other reason just as into the spider  verse introduced audiences to the idea  of using cartoon  physics as actual superpowers so too  have captain carrot and his furry  friends enjoyed a long history of  turning their slapstick toughness into a  tremendous advantage  take the events of the entirely straight  faced the multiversity series  in which carrot is plucked from his own  universe to fight in a far more serious  one  beside heroes from more typical dc  domains  while they get burned cut and crushed he  is merely flattened into a coin  and springs back up again try that on  for size steppenwolf  the fourth world is one of the best  parts of the dc  mythos it's high drama psychedelic  science fiction  and pop mythology all rolled up in jack  kirby's techno fantasy aesthetic  characters like darkseid and mr miracle  have gone on to figure  ensearing post-modern family dramas and  vast interstellar sagas alike  luckily the fourth world's characters  are already set to be part of the dceu  in the new gods movie directed by ava  duvernay  but it's all pomp and circumstance when  it comes to the denizens of apocalypse  and new genesis  enter the forever people the flower  children from beyond the stars  bottom line there is nothing subtle  about the forever people  they spend their immortal lives zooming  over the electron road in their mother  box-powered super cycle  they have names like big bear beautiful  dreamer and mark moonrider  and they dress like they were way laid  at a power rangers convention on their  way to coachella  in a superhero landscape that tends  toward stainless steel and desaturation  the forever people could be a heady  breath of fresh air  telling a genuinely universal teenage  superhero story  they're young they're invincible and  they're all tangled up in the wars and  triumphs of the adults in their lives  it's a tale as old as time except for  the cosmic motorbike that is  is there any super team more beloved  than the justice league  these guys are to comic books what apple  pie is to pastry  booyah but justice league international  is not exactly the team you picture  when that iconic squad of superheroes  comes to mind  assembled in the wake of crisis on  infinite earths  the justice league international  couldn't really get a hold of superman  wonder woman or the flash they're  basically the b side of justice leagues  batman's there but he's practically  marooned in a sea of lesser known heroes  like  blue beetle dr fate and black canary  what results is a zany delight the  tension among these mismatched team  members is palpable  and the series unflappable sense of  humor remains a breath of fresh air  jli blends comedy with genuine heroics  and keeps both parts all the more fresh  by doing so  the dc eu has struggled with dour  po-fascidness in the past  so why not inject it with a little  laughter  trouble's afoot in the dc universe but  superman batman and wonder woman are  busy  so what's a terrified bystander to do  why  call the hero hotline of course  available 24 hours a day  the hero hotline will dispatch one of  its many qualified super associates to  take care of whatever you need  run by the mysterious coordinator the  hotline's heroes include  luminaries such as microwavable  zeep the living sponge and marie a  psychic turtle  sporting a truly adorable helmet as you  might have guessed  the heroes of the hotline are not  exactly the dc universe's  premier good guys but what a concept  for one the hero hotline is unbashably  corporate  offering a unique look at how a world  with superheroes might actually function  and though the hotline's roster isn't  exactly a-list  it's hard not to fall in love with them  microwave a bell  juggles inexact bus schedules alongside  her scientific exploits  mr muscle constantly changes his name  and stretch lives life with stretching  powers that never stop working  meaning he typically looks like a wad of  thoroughly chewed gum  this could easily be the dceu's  guardians of the galaxy moment  and would provide a fascinating new  perspective on superhero storytelling  the newsboy legion began in the golden  age as a group of orphans living in  metropolis's notorious slums  they're a scrappy rambunctious gang who  slinged papers and managed to get into  all sorts of thrilling trouble  going by nicknames like big words and  scrappy years later  they were reintroduced and mixed up in  the more scientific corners of the dc  universe  leading to a whole lot of stories about  newsboy legion clones getting involved  in all  different corners of the dc universe  they are in short  the most classic of comic book  inventions a pretty simple concept made  wildly weird  by continuity reinvention and science so  advanced as to border on magic  the dc eu has a ton of options to pursue  here  if they ever wanted to introduce the  newsboy legion they could always go  classic  after all who doesn't like newsies but  the newsboy legion's involvement with  the fourth world and government cloning  has been part of their story for just as  long as their g-whiz golden years  that's not even the end of it though  young justice outsiders  recently reimagined the legion as  composed of news girls  who stream from their phones instead of  slinging papers  audiences could fall in love with any of  these takes whether decidedly old school  or totally new it isn't exactly accurate  to say that the royal flesh gang have  worn many hats over the course of their  decades long history  they have always maintained their  playing card theme for example  they've always been bad guys and they've  always favored a sleek aesthetic  but within those parameters the  portrayals of this particular team have  varied  wildly over the years the royal flush  gang have been taken over by the joker  dabbled in mind control and been  revealed as a multi-generational  operation perpetuated by  one seriously villainous family  there's one take that the dceu should  pay particular attention to however  the royal flush gang as portrayed on  justice league  unlimited and one of the most affecting  scenes of the series  it is revealed that this incarnation of  the team was created by ace  a psychic teenager who has warped  innocent bystanders into filling out the  gang's ranks  batman is sent in to kill her before she  breaks reality  entirely but all ace wants is for  someone to listen to her  batman does and holds her hand until she  passes away naturally  a revamp of the gang with this take on  ace at its core  is practically begging to be put on the  big screen  her story confronts dc's heroes with  some genuinely hard truths  while complicating the villains around  her and for all that subversion  it's a choice that still allows for all  the stylish fun of classic gang  interpretations  as far as villains go the royal flush  gang is a winning hand  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  the dc eu are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one
 

